    "markdown": "![Hugging Face's logo](https://huggingface.co/front/assets/huggingface_logo-noborder.svg) Hugging Face⟨1⟩\n  *  Models ⟨2⟩\n  *  Datasets ⟨3⟩\n  *  Spaces ⟨4⟩\n  *  Buckets new⟨5⟩\n  *  Docs ⟨6⟩\n  *  Enterprise ⟨7⟩\n  * Pricing⟨8⟩\n  *     * Website\n      *  Tasks⟨9⟩\n      *  HuggingChat⟨10⟩\n      *  Collections⟨11⟩\n      *  Languages⟨12⟩\n      *  Organizations⟨13⟩\n    * Community\n      *  Blog⟨14⟩\n      *  Posts⟨15⟩\n      *  Daily Papers⟨16⟩\n      *  Hardware⟨17⟩\n      *  Learn⟨18⟩\n      *  Discord⟨19⟩\n      *  Forum⟨20⟩\n      *  GitHub⟨21⟩\n    * Solutions\n      *  Team & Enterprise⟨7⟩\n      *  Hugging Face PRO⟨22⟩\n      *  Enterprise Support⟨23⟩\n      *  Inference Providers⟨24⟩\n      *  Inference Endpoints⟨25⟩\n      *  Storage Buckets⟨5⟩\n  * * * *\n  * Log In⟨26⟩\n  * Sign Up⟨27⟩\n\n\n#   Datasets:⟨3⟩\n* * *\n ![](https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/636865b8cca0a0a962c21f3f/n1PEv1RXr_QrhK7DIZbOg.png) ⟨28⟩\nAI4Manufacturing⟨28⟩\n/\nD14-vision-qa⟨29⟩\nlike 2\nFollow\n![⟨30⟩] AI4Manufacturing 13\nModalities:  Image ⟨31⟩ Text ⟨32⟩\nFormats:  parquet ⟨33⟩\nSize:  1K - 10K ⟨34⟩\nArXiv:\narxiv: 2605.10865\nTags:  smart-manufacturing ⟨35⟩ industrial ⟨36⟩ vision ⟨37⟩ cad ⟨38⟩ benchmark ⟨39⟩ evaluation ⟨40⟩\nLibraries:  Datasets ⟨41⟩ pandas ⟨42⟩ Polars ⟨43⟩ + 1\nLicense:\nother\n Dataset card ⟨29⟩ Data Studio ⟨44⟩ Files Files and versions xet ⟨45⟩ Community ⟨46⟩\n##  You need to agree to share your contact information to access this dataset\nThis repository is publicly accessible, but you have to accept the conditions to access its files and content.\nThis dataset is released for **research use**. Please state your name, affiliation, and intended use.\nLog in⟨47⟩ or Sign Up⟨48⟩ to review the conditions and access this dataset content.\n  * Why this is not VLM training data⟨49⟩\n  * Intended uses⟨50⟩\n  * Schema⟨51⟩\n  * Provenance⟨52⟩\n\n\n#   ⟨53⟩ D14 Vision-QA — CAD visual question answering (evaluation benchmark) \nThe **Vision-QA layer** of D14 (BenchCAD), packaged separately with its intended usage made explicit: this is an **evaluation benchmark / agentic-setting seed, NOT direct VLM training data.**\n**2,400 records** : a 4-view orthographic render of a CAD part + a numeric question + the gold answer. The underlying CadQuery program that generated the part (and the answers) is preserved in `metadata.gt_code`.\n##   ⟨49⟩ Why this is not VLM training data \nBenchCAD's Vision QA is one half of a deliberate **matched-pair design** : the _same_ questions are asked given the image (vision QA) and given the CadQuery source (code QA), to _measure_ what vision alone can recover. Most questions ask about the **program structure** (\"how many `.workplane()` calls?\", \"on which line is the first hole operation?\") or **exact dimensions** (\"largest fillet radius?\") — information that is _not present in the pixels_. We verified this empirically with a blind-answerability probe (Claude Sonnet 5, 60 stratified questions, ±5% tolerance):  \n| question bucket  | share  | question-only  | + image  | + code  |  \n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |  \n| code-structure (op counts, line numbers…)  | ~48%  | 13%  | 20%  | **60%**  |  \n| exact metric (dims, ratios)  | ~23%  | 0%  | **0%**  | **60%**  |  \n| numeric-threshold comparisons  | ~17%  | 40%  | 40% _(no lift = prior/guessing)_  | 73%  |  \n| genuinely visual (shape family, visible counts)  | ~11%  | 40%  | **66%**  | 80%  |  \nOnly the _visual_ bucket gains real accuracy from the image. Training a VLM to \"reason\" its way to the other answers from a render would teach it to fabricate measurements and code facts — so the `reasoning` field is intentionally left `null` here, while the two trainable D14 layers (image→code generation and code editing) are annotated separately.\n##   ⟨50⟩ Intended uses \n  1. **Evaluation** : benchmark multimodal CAD understanding; the vision-vs-code accuracy gap per bucket is the interesting measurement (per the matched-pair design).\n  2. **Agentic setting** : with tools, all buckets become answerable — e.g. an agent that retrieves the part's program (`metadata.gt_code`) or executes/measures the geometry, then answers. The image+question+gold triples are ready-made tasks for such a loop.\n  3. **Open-book QA** : providing `metadata.gt_code` alongside the image turns every record into a well-posed code-comprehension question (BenchCAD's \"code QA\" modality).\n\n\n##   ⟨51⟩ Schema   \n| field  | content  |  \n| --- | --- |  \n| `query`  | the question  |  \n| `image`  | 4-view orthographic render (PNG)  |  \n| `annot`  | `{\"answer\", \"level\" (L1–L6), \"qa_id\", \"source\", \"type\" (integer/dim/ratio)}`  |  \n| `reasoning`  |  `null` (deliberately — see above)  |  \n| `metadata`  | provenance + **`gt_code`**(the CadQuery program; ground truth for all answers)  |  \nScoring convention (from BenchCAD): exact match for integers, ±5% tolerance for dims/ratios. Boolean golds are encoded as integers: yes = 1, no = 0.\n##   ⟨52⟩ Provenance \nExtracted unchanged from `AI4Manufacturing/benchcad_TB3E1_D14` (split `QA`), which converts **BenchCAD** (arXiv:2605.10865) into the unified Smart-Manufacturing SFT schema. Please cite BenchCAD if you use this dataset.\nCopy to bucket new \n\nDownloads last month\n    29\nTotal file size: 50.9 MB\n##  Paper for AI4Manufacturing/D14-vision-qa\n#### BenchCAD: A Comprehensive, Industry-Standard Benchmark for Programmatic CAD Paper • 2605.10865 • Published May 12 • 1 ⟨54⟩\nSystem theme\nCompany\nTOS⟨55⟩ Privacy⟨56⟩ About⟨57⟩ Careers⟨58⟩ ⟨1⟩\nWebsite\nModels⟨2⟩ Datasets⟨3⟩ Spaces⟨4⟩ Pricing⟨8⟩ Docs⟨6⟩\n",
